{
  "about": [
    "The piece envelope's rules as one table, run by the backend's events package (envelope_test.go) and by the site's mock (tests/unit/event-sources-mock.test.ts, from a copy at tests/unit/__fixtures__/event-pieces.json). Change both with it.",
    "Each case sends pieces to a source that holds schema (field to type), or schema_fields fields f1 to fN that are all numbers, or none, under limits. A refusal's piece is the place, from 1, of the piece it refuses, and 0 when it refuses the send as a whole.",
    "A piece's data is data_json (its exact text), data_base64 (bytes that are not UTF-8) or data_size (the object {\"s\":\"aaa...\"} of exactly that many bytes). repeat stands for that many pieces with the id followed by 1, 2, and so on. occurred_at is RFC 3339 text, read before the other rules.",
    "want is a refusal (refused: invalid or fields, and its message) or what the send stores: bytes (its batch object, uncompressed), new_fields by name, and the schema after it (or schema_fields, its size).",
    "text_fields are the rules of a source's text field (Go's Schema.WithText, run by schema_test.go): each names text_field on a source that holds schema and, beside it, schema_fields fields f1 to fN that are all numbers, under limits' max_fields. want is a refusal (refused: invalid or fields, and its message) or the schema after it (or schema_fields, its size), which always holds text_field as a string."
  ],
  "limits": {
    "max_pieces_per_send": 500,
    "max_send_bytes": 1048576,
    "max_piece_bytes": 262144,
    "max_fields": 200
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "accepts ids of 0x21 and 0x7E",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "id": "!",
          "data_json": "{}"
        },
        {
          "id": "~",
          "data_json": "{}"
        }
      ],
      "want": {
        "new_fields": [],
        "schema": {},
        "bytes": 130
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "accepts an id with a quote and a backslash",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "id": "a\"b\\c",
          "data_json": "{}"
        }
      ],
      "want": {
        "new_fields": [],
        "schema": {},
        "bytes": 71
      }
    },
    {
